    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented and verified.\n\n## Result\n\n- `mvn test` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 2/2 tests pass, including the new `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (expects 409) and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (expects 2xx).\n\nNote: `mvn verify` fails only at the JaCoCo coverage gate (line coverage ~9% vs. required 85%). This is a pre-existing condition \u2014 the repo's entire test tree is just the two acceptance tests, which can't cover 85% of a large codebase regardless of my change. My change adds coverage rather than removing it (the conflict path is now exercised); the test suite itself is green.\n\n## Changes\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md:\n\n1. **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added `Collection<Owner> findByTelephone(String telephone)` to the interface, implemented in all three profiles:\n   - `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (active `spring-data-jpa`): `@Query` by telephone\n   - `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl` (`jpa`): EntityManager query\n   - `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl` (`jdbc`): named-parameter SQL\n\n2. **New pipeline step** `EnsureUniqueTelephone` \u2014 reads the already-normalized `@Val Owner` (BuildOwner strips non-digits before this step), looks up existing owners by telephone, and throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` if any *other* owner uses it. The id guard makes it reusable for updates too; on create the id is null so any match counts.\n\n3. **Wired into `owners.POST.yml`** between `build` and `save` (`build \u2192 ensureUniqueTelephone \u2192 save \u2192 respond`), under the same `transaction` governance \u2014 so the duplicate check reads within the request transaction and rejects before persisting.\n\n4. **New escalation**: `DuplicateTelephoneException extends Exception` + `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler` returning **409 CONFLICT** as a `ProblemDetail` (matching the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` handler's shape, with `errors: [\"telephone\"]`), registered via `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`.\n\nThe check runs against the normalized telephone, so inputs like `608-555-1023` and `6085551023` collide and the second create returns 409, as required.",
